"US-0034 (EPIC-00, docs/features/epic-00-fixes.md): Linux update fails with \"Command failed: pkexec dpkg -i <file>\"; in a shell the same command says \"pkexec must be setuid root\", earlier releases prompted for the password. Run /usr/bin/pkexec /usr/bin/dpkg by absolute path, show the real reason (stderr last line / exit code) instead of the Command failed line, and when pkexec cannot prompt show the sudo apt install command with the full file path. Hotfix, ships alone as v0.2.12."
